# examples/regressions/native_union_known_stop — THE NATIVE BACKEND'S NULL-UNION STOP, PROMOTED.
#
# Owner ruling 2026-07-28: *"é trocar a asserção para esperar por falha honesta e não skippar ou
# comentar, perfeito. Pode providenciar, atacamos na .32."*
#
# CLOSED, cargo/0.3.1.0-null-adopt (0.3.1.0) — measured, not guessed: `probe()` now returns 42 on
# BOTH routes (`TEKO_BACKEND=c` and the default native backend). The doc below (WHY A WHOLE PROJECT,
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY BROKEN) is kept VERBATIM as the historical record the "promote to a positive
# scenario the day it closes" convention (`diagnostics.tkr`'s own known-stop shape) asks for; only
# the `Scenario` at the bottom changed, from `When compilation fails` to `When built and run`.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY CLOSED IT. Not the full `.32` porting this file originally called for (the C
# emitter's `UnionRepr` = Niche | InlineTag | BoxInArena dial has NOT been ported to the native
# backend — every union here is still the one uniform `tag@0 + payload@8` shape,
# `null_union_shape`'s own doc in `src/lir/lower.tks`). What closed THIS scenario is narrower and
# was found while fixing an unrelated gap (`a != null`/`a == null` over an explicit `T | null`
# variant not compiling on either route, cargo/0.3.1.0-null-adopt): `lower_cast` unconditionally
# asked `prim_kind_of` for its cast's OWN type, which has no single machine class for a `Variant` —
# but a cast whose resolved type IS a `Variant` is never a user `to` (the checker restricts `to` to
# numeric/char/bool); it is the synthetic widening node the const inliner (`widen_inlined_const`,
# #630) wraps a `let`-bound scalar-const reference in when the reference's declared union type
# differs from its substituted (narrower, member-typed) initializer — EXACTLY the shape `present`/
# `absent` below take once inlined. `lower_cast` now routes a `Variant`-targeted cast through
# `lower_value_into_type` (this backend's placement-aware coercion, the analog of the C emitter's
# `cg_cast_target_is_variant` -> `emit_as`) instead of `prim_kind_of`, which is what makes THIS
# specific shape (a numeric null-union reached through the const-inliner's widen) lower correctly.
# The general `.32` porting (comparing/lowering a null-union through EVERY placement a `UnionRepr`
# dial would touch) is not claimed done by this — only this one shape is verified.
#
# NOT MOVED BACK TO `bulk` — UPDATE (cargo/0.3.1-dissolver-bulk, 2026-07-29): the day-it-closes
# instruction below (and the "WHY A WHOLE PROJECT" comparison after it) named `bulk` as the eventual
# destination for the positive scenario. `examples/regressions/bulk` no longer exists at all — owner
# ruling 2026-07-29 dissolved it: its 214 files were never distributed among the ten permitted
# regression channels, and the corpus that survived triage moved into the channels that fit it
# (`examples/regressions/own_native` chief among them). This scenario STAYS in its own project —
# promoted here is exactly as strong a guarantee as a positive row anywhere else, and this project
# already exists and already gates `teko test .`, so there is no reason left to relocate it.
#
# WHY A WHOLE PROJECT FOR ONE SCENARIO, and it is not tidiness — the two existing homes both
# structurally refuse it:
#
#   `bulk.tkr`         every scenario runs off ONE SUCCESSFUL build. A shape that cannot be lowered
#                      does not merely fail its own row, it takes the other 196 with it — which is
#                      exactly what it did, hiding every one of them behind a single line.
#   `diagnostics.tkr`  every scenario runs off ONE FAILING build, but those ~70 cases fail in the
#                      CHECKER. The build dies there and never reaches the backend, so a stop pinned
#                      here would never fire: a test that cannot fail is not a test.
#
# So it gets its own project, whose single build fails in the BACKEND with nothing else competing to
# fail first.
#
# NOT COMMENTED, NOT SKIPPED, and that distinction is the whole point. A commented fixture is a
# silent skip wearing a different hat — it stops asking the question, and nothing ever tells you the
# answer changed. This scenario keeps ASSERTING, on every run: it demands the exact stop the backend
# produces today.
#
# THE DAY THE .32 CLOSES IT, THIS GOES RED. The build will succeed, `When compilation fails` will not
# be satisfied, and the suite will say so loudly. That failure is the SIGNAL to promote this back to
# what it was — `When built and run` / `Then exit = 42` — IN THIS SAME PROJECT (`bulk` is gone; see
# the UPDATE note above). The same shape `diagnostics.tkr` already uses for its own known-stop:
# *"promote to a positive scenario the day it closes"*.
#
# WHAT IS ACTUALLY BROKEN, measured (`examples/probes/match_shapes`, 29 shapes x 3 compilers):
#
#   - the stop is the CAST TARGET asking `prim_kind_of` for `u64 | null`, not the arithmetic — the
#     probe's `m03` has no arithmetic at all and stops identically;
#   - annotating the binding changes NOTHING (the `tNN` control group is identical to `mNN`), so the
#     checker's inference is not involved: the match's type really is `u64`;
#   - `bool | null` and `Box | null` LOWER today, so it is specific to a numeric member;
#   - the published 0.3.0.30 stops on this too, and on six shapes this train has since FIXED. The
#     gap has an origin, not an age — there is no regression to bisect.
#
# The root cause is named in `docs/design/null-as-union-type.md` terms: the C emitter picks a
# representation per declared type (`UnionRepr` = Niche | InlineTag | BoxInArena, keyed off
# `cg_type_is_niche_able` + `cg_type_min_bytes`), while the native backend has exactly one shape —
# `tag@0 + payload@8`, held by address. Porting that choice is the `.32` work.
Feature: native backend — a numeric null-union has no single PrimKind (CLOSED — cargo/0.3.1.0-null-adopt)

  # src/probe.tks — the body authored 2026-07-24 (`1201088`), unchanged since, and green through
  # the C route the whole time. The native backend now lowers it too (see the CLOSED note above).
  Scenario: a `to` cast whose match subject is a numeric null-union now lowers correctly
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "42"
